## Why Wi-Fi Is Better Than Bluetooth for TV Remote Control

Many people assume Bluetooth is the go-to wireless standard, but for TV remote control, Wi-Fi wins in most scenarios:

| Feature | Wi-Fi Remote | Bluetooth Remote |
|---|---|---|
| Range | 30+ meters (same network) | ~10 meters line-of-sight |
| Pairing | One-time PIN | Re-pairs frequently |
| Latency | Near-zero over LAN | 10–40ms typical |
| Works through walls | Yes | Reduced performance |
| Keyboard input | Full keyboard | Limited on most |
| Setup complexity | Simple, automatic | Device-dependent |

Because Wi-Fi remotes communicate over your local network rather than a direct radio link, walls and distance matter far less. You can control your TV from another room, which is genuinely useful for adjusting volume during ads.

